    "result_text": "The AcceptanceTest is the only test class (the others are support classes). The full suite is green.\n\nThe change is complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the owner read model, formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`.\n\n**1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `ownerSegment` property to the `OwnerDto` schema as a read-only string enum with the four allowed values (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`). This drives the openapi-generator to produce `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum` at build time, matching the existing pattern used for `ageBand`.\n\n**2. `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired a `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment` and added the `ownerSegment(Owner)` helper. It reuses the existing `membershipLevel(owner)` and `locality(owner)` logic:\n- **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n- **AREA** = `METRO` when locality is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL`.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS. Both acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known Sydney/NSW owner, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown-region owner) pass.",
